Subject: [SE3-P2] winedmo: activate all selected streams before starting

media_source_start() activated streams one at a time while the demux
thread was already reading, so the first packets of a later-index stream
could be dropped as belonging to an inactive stream (seen as a lost leading
ALAC block, worst case a lost first video GOP). Mark every selected stream
active under its queue lock before the per-stream start loop when starting
from STOPPED.

---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -1400,6 +1400,21 @@
         return hr;
     }
 
+    /* The demux thread reads once any stream is active and drops packets for
+     * inactive streams, so activate every selected stream before starting any:
+     * otherwise the leading packets of a later stream can be lost. */
+    if (starting)
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
+        {
+            struct media_stream *stream = source->streams[i];
+
+            EnterCriticalSection(&stream->queue_cs);
+            stream->active = !!descriptors[i];
+            LeaveCriticalSection(&stream->queue_cs);
+        }
+    }
+
     for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
     {
         struct media_stream *stream = source->streams[i];
